<title>USA: Leviathan Gas sees Q2 charge from properties.</title>
<headline>Leviathan Gas sees Q2 charge from properties.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leviathan Gas Pipeline Partners LP said on Monday that it expects a second quarter charge related to its investments in two non-producing properties.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement that it is taking a charge from certain gathering facilities associated with Tatham Offshore Inc's Ship Shoal Block 331 and Ewing Bank Block 914 2 well.</p>
<p>The expected charges to income are of a non-recurring and non-cash nature and therefore do not impact cash flows, the company said.</p>
</text>
